    "body": "A corrupt `blocks/index` can stop the node at startup. A last block file number of -1 makes it read before the start of a vector. A very large one makes it allocate and read that many file infos. A block without a parent, or with a parent at the wrong height, hits the assert in `CBlockIndex::GetAncestor`.\n\nI reject these entries on load, so init reports the usual database error and suggests `-reindex`. A last file without stored info is still accepted when the file before it has info, because running out of disk space while opening a new file leaves that state. The new unit tests fail on master, and the reindex, pruning and assumeutxo functional tests pass. #32427 would replace this database and derive the last file number from its entries.\n\nThis is one of several PRs from a large audit of Bitcoin Core that I did with the help of LLM tools. The audit produced its evidence all at once, which is why the PRs arrive together. I understand each change fully and will answer review questions myself.\n",
