      "message": "blockstorage: validate last file and parent links\n\nA last block file number of -1 in blocks/index makes the node read\nbefore the start of a vector. A very large one makes it allocate and\nread that many file infos. A block without a parent, or with a parent at\nthe wrong height, hits the assert in CBlockIndex::GetAncestor.\n\nI reject a negative number. I also reject a last file number when\nneither that file nor the one before it has stored file info. The file\nbefore is enough because the node can claim a new file and run out of\ndisk space before writing to it. Every block above genesis must have a\nparent at the previous height. Loading then fails with an error, and the\nnode asks for -reindex. Unit tests cover each case.",
